{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-97542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "An object moves along a circular path with position $r(t)=3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j)$ meters. Find the magnitude of the acceleration of the object at time $t,$ measured in seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we find the velocity vector by differentiating the position vector. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =(r(t))^{′} \\\\  & =(3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j))^{′} \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the acceleration vector by differentiating the velocity vector. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =(v(t))^{′} \\\\  & =(-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j)^{′} \\\\  & =-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the magnitude of the acceleration as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}||a(t)|| & =\\sqrt{(-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}+(-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144{cos}^{2}⁡2t+144{sin}^{2}⁡2t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144} \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude of the acceleration is $12\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nNote that $||a||$ is constant, but $a$ is not. \n\n**Method 2**\n\nFor uniform circular motion in the $xy$-plane, we have\n\n$$\na=-{\\omega }^{2}r\\,⇒\\,||a||={\\omega }^{2}||r||.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the radius of the circle is $a=3\\,\\text{m}$ and the angular frequency $\\omega =2\\,\\text{rad/s}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n||a||={2}^{2}\\cdot 3=12\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b8e17431416efee0e02c850b9999add86038e40e00c2a2f7e86f15d44fd27c23"} {"question" "q-97542" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97542" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12{\\text{ m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "24{\\text{ m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "3{\\text{ m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "6{\\text{ m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "9{\\text{ m/s}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97542" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12{\\text{ m/s}}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97640" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "An object moves along a circular path with position $r(t)=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j$ meters. Find the speed of the object at time $t,$ measured in seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97640" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we find the velocity vector by differentiating the position vector. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =(r(t))^{′} \\\\  & =(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j)^{′} \\\\  & =-10\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed, we calculate the magnitude of the velocity vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}||v(t)|| & =\\sqrt{(-10\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)^{2}+(10\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100{sin}^{2}⁡2t+100{cos}^{2}⁡2t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100({sin}^{2}⁡2t+{cos}^{2}⁡2t)} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of the object is $10\\text{ m/s}.$\n\nNote that the speed is constant, but the velocity is not. \n\n**Method 2**\n\nFor uniform circular motion in the $xy$-plane, we have\n\n$$\n||v||=R|\\omega |,\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the radius of the circle, and $\\omega $ is the angular velocity.\n\nIn our case, the radius of the circle is $R=5\\,\\text{m}$ and the angular frequency $\\omega =2\\,\\text{rad/s}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n||v||=5\\cdot |2|=10\\text{ m/s}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97640" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b8e17431416efee0e02c850b9999add86038e40e00c2a2f7e86f15d44fd27c23"} {"question" "q-97640" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97640" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "100\\text{ m/s}"] ["math" "10\\text{ m/s}"] ["math" "20\\text{ m/s}"] ["math" "25\\text{ m/s}"] ["math" "5\\text{ m/s}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97640" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10\\text{ m/s}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97664" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along a counterclockwise circular path centered at $O$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity of $1\\,\\text{rad/s}.$ Given that the particle is located at $(5,0)$ when $t=0,$ find the velocity of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97664" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $R$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and the particle is at the position $(R,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nIn our case, we have $R=5$ and $\\omega =1\\text{ rad/s},$ so we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =5(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the velocity vector by differentiating the position vector. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =(5(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j))^{′} \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the velocity vector at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,i+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,j \\\\  & =-5\\,i\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97664" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b8e17431416efee0e02c850b9999add86038e40e00c2a2f7e86f15d44fd27c23"} {"question" "q-97664" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97664" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5\\,i"] ["math" "-5\\,i+5\\,j"] ["math" "-5\\,j"] ["math" "5\\,i"] ["math" "5\\,i-5\\,j"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97664" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5\\,i"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along a counterclockwise circular path centered at $O$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity of $2\\,\\text{rad/s}.$ Given that the particle is located at $(4,0)$ when $t=0,$ find the velocity of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $R$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and the particle is at the position $(R,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nIn our case, we have $R=4$ and $\\omega =2\\text{ rad/s},$ so we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the velocity vector by differentiating the position vector. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =(4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j))^{′} \\\\  & =-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the velocity vector at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{8},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8})\\,i+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8})\\,j \\\\  & =-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,i+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,j \\\\  & =-\\frac{8\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,i+\\frac{8\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,j \\\\  & =-4\\sqrt{2}\\,i+4\\sqrt{2}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b8e17431416efee0e02c850b9999add86038e40e00c2a2f7e86f15d44fd27c23"} {"question" "q-97666" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97666" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4\\sqrt{2}i+4\\sqrt{2}j"] ["math" "-4i+4\\sqrt{2}j"] ["math" "-8\\sqrt{2}j"] ["math" "4\\sqrt{2}i"] ["math" "4\\sqrt{2}i-4j"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97666" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4\\sqrt{2}i+4\\sqrt{2}j"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along a counterclockwise circular path centered at $O$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity of $0.5\\,\\text{rad/s}.$ Given that the particle is located at $(4,0)$ when $t=0,$ find the acceleration of the particle at $t=\\pi $ seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $a$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=a(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and the particle is at the position $(a,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=4$ and $\\omega =\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ rad/s},$ so we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,i+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the velocity and acceleration vectors by differentiating. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & ={(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,i+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,j)}^{′} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,j \\\\ a(t) & ={(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,j)}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the acceleration vector at $t=\\pi ,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(\\pi ) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,j \\\\  & =-\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b8e17431416efee0e02c850b9999add86038e40e00c2a2f7e86f15d44fd27c23"} {"question" "q-97674" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97674" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\,i+2\\,j"] ["math" "-\\,j"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}\\,i"] ["math" "2\\,j"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\,j"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"} {"question" "q-97674" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\,j"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076581/state.json" "file_sha256" "9cb0d45f8d53e346329a384c569b84e0a4d6173d03a729389b77659fa925acbb"}] "usage" {"q-97542" []} "basis" 2788 "retractions" [[17592186172578